---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro'
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro'
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../components/schema/BreadcrumbSchema.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — point.dog Digital"
  description="How point.dog collects, uses, and protects information."
>
  <BreadcrumbSchema items={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', url: '/privacy' }]} />

  <Hero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle={`Last updated: April 2026`}
    tone="primary"
  />

  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <Prose>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you contact us through the form on this site, we collect: your name, email
        address, optional company name, what you're after, and your message. That's it. We
        do not buy or sell contact lists.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use your information solely to respond to your inquiry. If we end up working
        together, your data goes into our project management system. If we don't end up
        working together, we may keep your information for follow-up but will honor any
        request to delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Tracking on this site</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Tag Manager and a first-party tracking pixel to understand how
        visitors find and use this site. This helps us measure the effectiveness of our
        own marketing — exactly what we'd build for our clients.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not run third-party advertising trackers from data brokers. The pixel is
        ours, the data is ours, and we don't share or sell it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use cookies for analytics, attribution, and to remember your preferences across
        sessions. You can disable cookies in your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:mike@point.dog">mike@point.dog</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </section>
</Layout>
